    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1277">

                <pb facs="1239" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg953"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2659</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-03T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3487. Your 4482, June 21, 3 p. m. Department regrets that you expressed yourself
                    to the Spanish Ambassador in such a way as to <pb facs="1240" n="954"
                        xml:id="pg954"/> give him the impression that you agreed as to the inutility
                    of presenting the German reply to the British Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
